HA! I finally did it!

 I had been playing NH for about two years now, mostly not surviving
long after the mines. My biggest achievment until recently was a priest
who found Mojo in the dungeons early on. He got whacked to death with it
on the quest, because some demon (don't remember the species) stole it
with a bullwhip, while a succubus distracted him.
 I usually like to play wizards, priests, rogues or rangers, but I quickly 
found out that the good old dwarven valkyrie has the highest survivability.

 I was pretty surprised that this one (the second try after the decision
to play wombats) made it to the quest so quickly. Probably I had been
reaching a critical mass of playing experience or something.

 I had been dipping Excalibur as soon as possible, but soon exchanged it
for Mjollnir which I got after the last charge of the second /oCM at an
altar on DL4. I did Soko before the mines (a habit that has saved many
lives, but probably was unneccesarry in this case) and got a BoH.
Minetown altar was cross-aligned. Got the stone from the catacombs and
went back out. There were quite few vaults in this game, so it was a
long time until I bought some protection. A throne on DL13 granted a
wish -> +0 GDSM. A sergeant in a barracks on DL20 yielded a silver saber; 
at that point I started twoweaponing it with Mojo. I drank 2 !oGL and 
went back to the quest portal.
 Home2 had both [GoP and a [CoDisplacement lying around. Both
accompanied me throughout the rest of the game. Also I learned to enjoy
the Mojo-Yoyo (sp?). Also found a /oPoly there and emptied it on Spot,
my large cat. He never turned into anything more dangerous until the
last shot turned him into a large dog. Well, so be it.
 The Quest was surprisingly easy, Lord Surtr escaped upstairs and then
died after a few whacks.

 On Medusas (peaceful Titan) my /oCold ran out, so I left Spot behind,
dug down and came back up with a towel around my head. Medusa took some
hits end escaped downstairs, but was quickly disposed of. The statue of
Perseus had [oLev and a [SoR. I didn't have a magic whistle yet, so Spot
still had to stay behind.

 On the castle I stashed my silver saber and put on the [AoR.
Masterminded the passtune, engraved the E-Word (first time this game)
and shredded monsters with the drawbridge (works extremely well). After
that the castle was quickly emptied. The /WoW went for: ?oCharging,
speed boots, "AoR, magic marker. Enchanted some of my armor and weapons.
I still didn't feel ready for gehennom (see previous thread) and went
rummaging through all of the Dungeon + the Mines. Turned Spot into an
arch-lich in the process, but he wasn't much help. Lugged him around
anyways for fear of him getting untame.
 I bought a ?oCharging in Minetown, blessed it and found out that you
can only enchant a magic marker once.

 Finally I entered Gehennom (scary place, that). A Marilith summoned
Yeenoghu on DL30. Fell through a hole in Asmodeus' Lair and landed in
Juiblex' swamp. Generally the big &s died surprisingly easy. Juiblex
t'ported next to me and died in two hits without attacking once.
Somewhere around this point I got another magic marker, wrote up the
rest of my gear including the silver saber (which was at +3 then) and
Excalibur and started wielding these two. Helped a lot against fire
traps. I only used Mojo for throwing it to a master mind flayer now and
then. I got sucked by those twice. Around DL36 I found a Hawaiian Shirt
and finally a =oTC to make my Orb useful as an escape item.

 It was only until DL45 that I found a =oFA. I cleared out Gehennom
until DL51, dug some tunnels through the mazes, reexplored a total of 16
levels (damned MMFs) and got into some serious summoning trouble at the
castle where I had abandoned spot. Arch liches generally gave me quite
some hard time. The rest was pretty straight forward. Killed Rodney, ran
down, got double troubled twice. Rodney sure is a tough guy, I only
death-rayed him once, then I was out of charges. Did the ritual.
 Used conflict and a /oSDD in the sanctum, which made it quite quick.
Took the amulet and hurried up. The mysterious force pulled me down 7
levels in total (not too much).

 Although I had no charges for the orb and no ?oGD, I found all the
portals pretty quickly. Air-Es gave me a hard time, but with conflict
and healing up in energy vortices it was not too hard.

 Took the ring of conflict off in water in case I should stumble upon
the portal. Slipped it on again pretty soon in astral because I really
didn't see another way to survive those massive hordes of monsters.

 /oTeleport helped a bit, and it took me some time to get the idea of
kicking down doors instead of opening then so I could move diagonally. I
spent ages being whacked by nasties while standing in blocked doorways.
 Went for the right altar first, guarded by pestilence (I almost
exclusively used /oTeleport on the riders, and generally a lot on
astral). Chaotic. Then to the middle one: Death (scary), neutral. OK, up
to the left one. Had a hard time getting past Famine, but finally I stood
on the altar and...

